phishy (high risk):-

IP-Based (Classic Hack): http://192.168.1.1/secure-login
Why: Legitimate companies use domain names (like google.com), never raw numbers.

Typosquatting: http://www.paypa1.com/verify
Why: Uses a 1 instead of an l. To a human eye it looks real, but your code flags it.

Subdomain Trick: http://amazon.security-update.net/account
Why: The real domain here is security-update.net, not Amazon.







Suspicious (Medium Risk) :-

URL Shorteners: https://bit.ly/3yXz9Qw or https://tinyurl.com/auth-check
Why: Shorteners hide the final destination. In a security context, a hidden destination is a red flag.

Suspicious Keywords: http://my-service.com/login-verify-banking
Why: Even if the domain is new, having "banking" or "verify" in the path increases the score in your analyze_links logic.






Safe (Low Risk) :-

Direct Official Link: https://www.google.com/settings

Standard Service: https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365

Company Portal: https://help.netflix.com/en/node/12345